{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1353908-god-machine-and-splinters-question","id":1353908,"title":"God-Machine and Splinters question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-09T11:31:14-08:00","id":1353908,"title":"God-Machine and Splinters question","content":"I noticed that the Seattle storyline focuses mostly on Splinters, i.e. locations where people can travel to other timelines. Is there any additional information on how these Splinters work?<br /> <br /> Questions I have so far:<ul><li>Are Splinters a common thing for the God-Machine to create or are they a specific feature of Seattle?</li> <li>Are Splinters only timelines from the past or can they be the future as well?</li> <li>Does time pass at the same speed as the primary timeline? Or can it be faster? Such as spending a year in 1920, but only a day has past in 2019.</li> <li>How important do you feel Splinters are to Demon the Descent?</li> <li>How have you incorporated Splinters into your game?</li> <li>How do people access Splinters? I know the intro mission in the Core Book says access is through a VW Beetle, but are there other examples of Splinter access points?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T13:50:47-08:00","id":1353951,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>Neither common nor unique. Time splinters aren't such a standard tool in the God-Machine's toolkit that demons are regularly used to dealing with them (usually; in addition to demons hanging around exception points like Seattle, also see below), but nothing prevents it from creating them outside of Seattle.</li> <li>Yes, the God-Machine can fracture time to link the future to the present.</li> <li>Nothing seems guaranteed or universal about time splinters. It is certainly conceivable that timelines might exist at rates of progression at odds with one another.</li> <li>Splinters are not very important to Demon: the Descent, in the sense that they're not a universal game conceit. The Seattle book deals with them, and does some fun stuff with them. They are a tool available in the Storyteller's toolkit, but it is very easy to run a Demon game that never calls for taking out that particular tool. They can, of course, be very important to individual games of Demon, such as those set in places like Seattle with an unusual proliferation of splinter timelines.</li> <li>My home games have not incorporated splinters.</li> <li>The God-Machine's occult physics are sufficiently complicated and strange that about anything can likely serve as a particular fracture's entry or exit point, though a given fracture <i>probably</i> doesn't have many different &quot;doors.&quot; Demon: Interface, a collection of short stories with brief relevant mechanical writeups attached to each story, includes a story about a fallen angel whose role for the Machine was to ensure intended futures by eliminating targets representing alternate possibilities. The mechanical writeup includes his Multiversal Antenna demonic form ability, which he uses to scry alternate arcs through time, and which can identify available entrances to splinter timelines.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 12-09-2019, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T13:59:00-08:00","id":1353954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1353908-god-machine-and-splinters-question#post1353908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed that the Seattle storyline focuses mostly on Splinters, i.e. locations where people can travel to other timelines. Is there any additional information on how these Splinters work?<br /> <br /> Questions I have so far:<ul><li>Are Splinters a common thing for the God-Machine to create or are they a specific feature of Seattle?</li> <li>Are Splinters only timelines from the past or can they be the future as well?</li> <li>Does time pass at the same speed as the primary timeline? Or can it be faster? Such as spending a year in 1920, but only a day has past in 2019.</li> <li>How important do you feel Splinters are to Demon the Descent?</li> <li>How have you incorporated Splinters into your game?</li> <li>How do people access Splinters? I know the intro mission in the Core Book says access is through a VW Beetle, but are there other examples of Splinter access points?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>1. Splinters are as common as a ST wants them to be. As an ST, I would not have them show up every week like a &quot;monster of the week&quot; thing but maybe every few chapters.<br /> 2. Splinters are reality off-shoots. They often loop time but do not have to be from any specific time if desired. So a repeating day for example could have been repeating for the last 10 years trying to resolve itself. Or, it could be of a future that never existed that is trying to &quot;come into being&quot;.<br /> 3. I haven't seen anything stating that time passes faster or slower. so I'd say that time will pass generally at the same speed. However, if access to a particular Splinter shows up in the Hedge, it could complicate things. If you want something different, go for it.<br /> 4. I played a game where only 1 Splinter showed up. Granted, the game was of mixed genre (Mages, Demons and Vamps) so it was not a focus. If you are doing a Demon-only standard game, then it could be as important as you make it. Perhaps a Splinter is trying to come into being and it's working against the God-Machine, threatening all reality. That is pretty important.<br /> 5. In my game, a Splinter opened up in response to a Mage-related issue where they were making a bomb to threaten reality. The G-M then made the Splinter to stop the bomb from coming to pass.<br /> 6. It can be accessed from anywhere. Generally, use Infrastructure to access as it is directly related to the G-M. Perhaps it's a door to a closet in a house but you have to open it while holding another object?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","name":"Ghostdriver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14512_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}